## 4. Manual End-to-End GUI Test Matrix

Manual GUI tests are executed using two browser windows (Google Chrome Normal vs. Google Chrome Incognito) connected to `http://localhost:3000`. These tests verify visual and interactive behaviors that are not testable via API calls.

| Test ID | Scenario & Functional Area | Test Steps | Observed GUI Behavior | Status |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: |
| **TC-MAN-01** | **Server IP & Port Configuration** | Open Server Config dialog → change port → save. | Modal saves configuration to `localStorage`, base URL updates dynamically. | **PASS** |
| **TC-MAN-02** | **Quick IM Login (No Auth)** | Navigate to "Quick IM" tab → enter username `alice_test` → click Join. | Instant login without password, session stored, redirect to `/chats`. | **PASS** |
| **TC-MAN-03** | **Active Users Real-Time Presence** | Login as Alice and Bob in separate browser windows. | Bob appears in Active Users tab with a green presence badge. | **PASS** |
| **TC-MAN-04** | **1-Click Direct Chat Spawn** | In Active Users tab, click "Chat" button on Bob's entry. | 1-on-1 chat window opens instantly with zero page reload. | **PASS** |
| **TC-MAN-05** | **Real-Time Message Delivery** | Alice sends a text message to Bob while both are online. | Message appears instantly on Bob's screen; Alice's checkmark changes to double gray (✓✓). | **PASS** |
| **TC-MAN-06** | **Read Receipt Synchronization** | Bob opens the chat window with Alice. | Alice's checkmarks change from gray to blue/cyan (✓✓) in real-time. | **PASS** |
| **TC-MAN-07** | **Multiple Simultaneous Conversations** | Alice opens a group chat while chatting with Bob. | Incoming group messages trigger a green badge number without disrupting the Bob chat. | **PASS** |
| **TC-MAN-08** | **Real-Time Typing Indicators** | Bob begins typing in the message input without sending. | Animated three-dot typing bubble appears on Alice's screen and disappears when Bob stops. | **PASS** |
| **TC-MAN-09** | **Idle & Away State Transitions** | Minimize browser tab or leave no interaction for 2 minutes. | Presence indicator dot changes from green (Online) to yellow/orange (Away). | **PASS** |
| **TC-MAN-10** | **Group Chat Lifecycle & Audit Trail** | Create group, invite members, then a member leaves the group. | Group is created; when member leaves, a system message `"User left the group"` appears. | **PASS** |

